    "resource_exhaustion - ApoDiceSolve.checkLevel():29-98 is an exponential brute-force solver, but it runs only on the user's OWN editor grid (ApoDiceEditor.solveLevel():171-181, triggered solely by the 'solve' button) with a working bBreak cancel flag; downloaded user-levels are never solved locally, so no remote trigger exists. Secondary theoretical issue: the readLine() loop at ApoDiceUserlevelsLoad.java:182-207 caps neither record count nor line length, so a hostile MITM streaming endless lines could grow the ArrayLists unbounded (heap exhaustion), but this requires the same attacker position as ApoDice-01 and is folded into that finding's scenario."
