  "notes": "This is the small Android ('apoDice4k') variant: 21 files total, ~3.7k LOC, all under net.apogames.apodice plus generated R/BuildConfig stubs. The security surface is narrow and entirely network-centric: two hardcoded http:// endpoints in ApoDiceConstants.java:5-6 feed an unvalidated text level format into a hand parser. The corpus-wide dangerous primitives (custom ClassLoader+defineClass, .cheat/.mar/.skunk/.rep binary parsers, MD5-highscore validation, ObjectInputStream, applet entry points, user.home path building) are NOT present in this variant - they belong to the desktop siblings; anyone attributing them to ApoDice would be wrong. Structural evidence of clone-and-own: ApoDiceUserlevelsLoad/ApoDiceUserlevels mirror the Apo<Userlevels>Load boilerplate seen across sibling variants (same 11-lines-per-record protocol, same singleton getInstance() pattern, same silent Exception swallowing at ApoDiceUserlevels.java:34-37 which masks malformed-server failures and quietly disables the userlevels feature), so fixing ApoDice-01/-02/-03 in this file family likely generalizes. Two environment caveats: (1) the archive nests a literal absolute path 'Users/eliahilse/Documents/GitHub/B/apogames/Android/ApoDice/' inside the target root; (2) the third-party bitsengine JAR sources are absent, so its networking/GL code could not be reviewed - all cited sinks are in first-party code. The bitsengine dependency also means runtime behavior (where uncaught exceptions land, thread death semantics) is inferred from standard Android/GLThread behavior, though the throwing code itself is unambiguous."
